          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:00:37Z",
          "note": "The {} empty legacy case returning undefined vs [] returning [] is intentional and documented in JSDoc. The asymmetry is behaviorally sound — {} means no credentials were ever configured (legacy absent state), whereas [] means credentials were explicitly cleared."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:00:37Z",
